  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1964-p27.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "By the triangle inequality, \\[|x-4|+|x-3|\\geq|4-3|=1.\\] Equality holds for every \\(x\\) between \\(3\\) and \\(4.\\) Therefore the strict inequality has a real solution exactly when \\(a\\gt1.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Interpret the sum as the distances from \\(x\\) to \\(3\\) and \\(4\\)",
        "Find its minimum for \\(3\\leq x\\leq4\\), remembering the inequality is strict"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
